  "source_commit": "ec9fa56b",
  "interpretation": "The welded circle and the spatial sets and unit tangent directions of all four boundary curves can be preserved by a smooth map. Preserving the full old parameterized boundary derivatives on both sides of each knot is impossible on three curves because their speed jumps at fixed continuous label. A smooth map that interpolates registered boundary knot positions and preserves the tangent directions must change the reference speed between some boundary knots."
